// Fuse pass lit tests (plan todo 14): elementwise producer-consumer chain
// fusion into one loop nest.
//
// The FUSE fixture computes z = tanh(a*x + b) as two elementwise loops over
// one shared iteration domain with an intermediate shared tensor; the pass
// merges them into ONE loop, rewrites the consumer's loads of the
// intermediate to the producer's stored value, and eliminates the
// intermediate (its alloc_shared is dead and erased). The BARRIER fixture is
// the identical chain with an atom.barrier between the loops (memory
// ordering: fusion must NOT fire). The MULTIUSE fixture gives the
// intermediate a second use outside the chain (fusion must NOT fire).

// RUN: kernelh-opt --load-atom %S/../../fixtures/passes/fuse.atom --run-passes=fuse --print-atom | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FUSED
// RUN: kernelh-opt --load-atom %S/../../fixtures/passes/fuse_barrier.atom --run-passes=fuse --print-atom | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BARRIER
// RUN: kernelh-opt --load-atom %S/../../fixtures/passes/fuse_multiuse.atom --run-passes=fuse --print-atom | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MULTIUSE

// The FUSE fixture collapses to ONE loop; the intermediate is gone before
// the loop (its alloc_shared would print there) and never reappears.
// FUSED-LABEL: atom.kernel @fuse(
// FUSED-NOT: atom.alloc_shared
// FUSED-COUNT-1: atom.loop_for
// FUSED: ^bb0(
// FUSED: atom.load
// FUSED: atom.mul
// FUSED: atom.load
// FUSED: atom.add
// FUSED: atom.math tanh
// FUSED: atom.store
// FUSED: atom.yield
// FUSED-NOT: atom.loop_for
// FUSED-NOT: atom.alloc_shared

// The BARRIER fixture keeps both loops with the barrier between them; a
// second atom.loop_for match after the barrier proves the consumer loop is
// intact.
// BARRIER-LABEL: atom.kernel @fuse_barrier(
// BARRIER: atom.alloc_shared
// BARRIER: atom.loop_for
// BARRIER: atom.store
// BARRIER: atom.barrier
// BARRIER: atom.loop_for
// BARRIER: atom.math tanh
// BARRIER: atom.store
// BARRIER: atom.yield
// BARRIER-NOT: atom.loop_for

// The MULTIUSE fixture keeps the intermediate's second use (the body load
// after the loops); two loops prove fusion did not fire.
// MULTIUSE-LABEL: atom.kernel @fuse_multiuse(
// MULTIUSE: atom.alloc_shared
// MULTIUSE-COUNT-2: atom.loop_for
// MULTIUSE: atom.load
// MULTIUSE: atom.math tanh
// MULTIUSE: atom.store
// MULTIUSE: atom.yield
// MULTIUSE: atom.load
// MULTIUSE-NOT: atom.loop_for
